{"version":1,"slug":"Others__General_Awareness_-_General_Studies_-_Super_Practice_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_69_(20Q)","path":"Others/General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 69 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 69 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If one of the interior angles of a regular polygon is 15/16 times of one of the interior angles of a regular decagon, then fine the number of diagonals of the polygon.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2342;&#2360;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; 15/16 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">35</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">35</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Interior angles of a regular polygon =15/16* [180*(10-2)/10]</p><p>[180*(n-2)/n] = 135</p><p>180n - 360 = 135n</p><p>45n = 360</p><p>n = 8</p><p>Number of diagonals of octagon = 8 * (8-3)/2 = 20</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a rhombus ABCD, O is any interior point such that OA = OC. What is five-ninths of the degree measure of &#8736;DOB?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, O &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; OA = OC &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;DOB &#2325;&#2375; &#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330;-&#2344;&#2380;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">120&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">150&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">90&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">90&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>As given a rhombus ABCD,OA=OC</p><p>As we know by the property of rhombus, it's diagonal bisect each other at right angle</p><p>As OA=OC,O lies in the perpendicular bisector of AC</p><p>So &#8736; AOB=&#8736; COD=90&deg; </p><p>&#8736; DOB=&#8736; AOB+&#8736; COD=180&deg; </p><p>So 5/9*180&deg; =100&deg; .</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the area of a quadrilateral ABCD, (shown below) in which sides AB and BC are equal, sides AD and CD are of lengths 5 cm and 13 cm, respectively, and side AD is perpendicular to the diagonal AC?</p><p><img width=255 height=161 id=\"Picture 30\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27933/image023.png\" ></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, (&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;) &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AB &#2324;&#2352; BC &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AD &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AD &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; AC &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=255 height=161 id=\"Picture 30\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27933/image023.png\" ></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">75 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">75 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">78 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">78 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">82 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">82 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">80 cm&#178;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">80 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;&#178;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>&#916;ADC: AD &#8869; AC, AD = 5, CD = 13, AC = &radic;(13&#178; - 5&#178;) = 12</p><p>Area &#916;ADC = (1/2)  X  12  X  5 = 30 cm&#178;</p><p>&#916;ABC: AB = BC, AC = 12</p><p>Area via Heron's: s = (10+10 + 12) / 2 = 16, Area = &radic;(16(6)(6)(4)]= 48cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total area = 30+48= 78 cm&#178;</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Let ABCD be a quadrilateral and AC, BD be diagonals. The length of BD = 20 cm and the heights of the triangles ABD and BCD are, respectively, 6 cm, 8 cm. Find the area of the quadrilateral ABCD (in cm<sup>2</sup>).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; ABCD &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; AC, BD &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; BD &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; = 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABD &#2324;&#2352; BCD &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">140</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">140</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">148</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">148</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1282</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1282</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>BD divides ABCD into triangles ABD and BCD.</p><p>Heights of &#8710;ABD = 6 cm </p><p>Heights of &#8710;BCD = 8 cm</p><p>Total area of ABCD = Area of &#8710;ABD + Area of &#8710;BCD</p><p>= &frac12; * 20 * 6 + &frac12; * 20 * 8 </p><p>= 140 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a quadrilateral ABCD, AB = BC, AD = DC. &#8736;ABD = 68&deg;, &#8736;ADB = (2y-7)&deg;, &#8736;BDC = 33&deg;, &#8736;DBC = (3x+2)&deg;. Then the value of 2x+3y is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB = BC, AD = DC. &#8736;ABD = 68&deg;, &#8736;ADB = (2y-7)&deg;, &#8736;BDC = 33&deg;, &#8736;DBC = (3x+2)&deg;. &#2340;&#2379; 2x+3y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">108</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">108</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">104</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">104</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">118</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">118</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>As ,AB = BC, AD = DC. &#8736;ABD = 68&deg;, &#8736;ADB = (2y-7)&deg;, &#8736;BDC = 33&deg;, &#8736;DBC = (3x+2)&deg;.</p><p>We have:-</p><p><img width=210 height=145 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27408/image024.png\"></p><p>In triangle ABD and in triangle DBC</p><p>AB = BC </p><p>AD = DC , and DB is common</p><p>So &#916;ABD is congruent to &#916;DBC (by SSS)</p><p>So , 3x+2= 68&deg; </p><p>x=22</p><p>and (2y -7)&deg; = 33</p><p>y=20</p><p>so 2x+3y = 2*22+3*20 = 104</p><p>option (c) is the correct answer. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>ABCD is a trapezium in which AB is parallel to CD, and E and F are the mid-points of non-parallel sides AD and BC. If EF is parallel to AB, AB = 28 cm and CD = 18 cm, then find EF (in cm).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>ABCD &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; AB, CD &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; E &#2324;&#2352; F &#2309;&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; AD &#2324;&#2352; BC &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;-&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; EF, AB &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, AB = 28 cm &#2324;&#2352; CD = 18 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; EF (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">23</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">46</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">46</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>If E and F are the mid-points of non-parallel sides AD and BC then:</p><p>EF= (AB +CD)/2</p><p>EF= (28 +18)/2</p><p>EF= 23 cm</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the given figure, &#916;QPS &#8773; &#916;SRQ. Find the measure of &#8736;PSR.</p><p><img width=220 height=205 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24204/image052.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#916;QPS &#8773; &#916;SRQ &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;PSR &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"220\" height=\"205\" id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24204/image052.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">64&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">74&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">74&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">52&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">52&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">82&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">82&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Since, </p><p>&#916;QPS &#8773; &#916;SRQ</p><p>Which means: </p><p>&#8736;QPS = &#8736;QRS, &#8736;PQS = &#8736;RSQ, and &#8736;PSQ = &#8736;RQS</p><p>&#8736;QPS = &#8736;QRS = 106&deg;</p><p>&#8736;PSQ = &#8736;RQS = 52&deg;</p><p>In &#916;SQR:</p><p>&#8736;RSQ = 180&deg;  -  106&deg;  -  52&deg; = 22&deg;</p><p>&#8736;PSR = &#8736;PSQ + &#8736;RSQ</p><p>= 52&deg; + 22&deg;</p><p>= 74&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A quadrilateral having equal diagonals and equal opposite sides is always a</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2360;&#2342;&#2376;&#2357; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">trapezium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">kite</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2340;&#2306;&#2327;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">rhombus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">rectangle</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2351;&#2340;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Equal opposite sides: parallelogram</p><p>Equal diagonals: rectangle (in parallelograms, diagonals equal only in rectangle)</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>WXYZ is a quadrilateral in which XQ and ZP are perpendicular to WY such that XQ = ZP. Diagonals ZX and WY intersect each other at point O. If OX = 12 cm, then find the value of ZX (in cm).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">WXYZ &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; XQ &#2324;&#2352; ZP, WY &#2346;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; XQ = ZP &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; ZX &#2324;&#2352; WY &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; O &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; OX = 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; ZX &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The figure representation of above question is :-</p><p><img width=200 height=124 id=\"Picture 20\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27167/image019.png\" ></p><p>As XQ = ZP and both are perpendicular to WY,</p><p>Here &#916;XQY and &#916;ZPY are congruent (by R.H.S)</p><p>So both triangles will have equal corresponding sides</p><p>So,</p><p>OX = OZ</p><p>As OX = 12 cm, So</p><p>OZ = 12 cm</p><p>Now for ZX:</p><p>Here,</p><p>ZX = OX + OZ</p><p>ZX = 12 cm + 12 cm</p><p>ZX = 24 cm</p><p>option (b) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the number of diagonals of a regular polygon, sum of whose interior angles is 2700&deg;.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 2700&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">121</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">121</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">119</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">119</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">127</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">127</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">117</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">117</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Number of sides whose sum of interior angles is 2700&deg; = 2700&#730;/180&#730; + 2 = 17</p><p>Number of diagonals = 17*(17-3)/2 = 119</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>ABCD is a square and &#9651;MAB is an equilateral triangle. MC and MD are joined. What is the degree measure of &#8736;MDC?</p><p><img width=101 height=116 id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image033.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>ABCD &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#9651;MAB &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; MC &#2324;&#2352; MD &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;MDC &#2325;&#2366; &#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"101\" height=\"116\" id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image033.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">78&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">78&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">65&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">65&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">75&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">75&#730;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=121 height=139 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image034.jpg\"></p><p>&#9651;MAB is an equilateral triangle, so AM = MB = AB</p><p>and ABCD is a square, so AB = BC = CD = DA</p><p>AM = AD</p><p>&#8736;AMD =&#8736;ADM</p><p>&#8736;MAD = 60&#730; + 90&#730; = 150&#730;</p><p>&#8736;AMD + &#8736;ADM =180&#730; - 150&#730; = 30&#730;</p><p>&#8736;ADM = 30&#730;/2 = 15&#730;</p><p>&#8736;MDC = 90&#730; - 15&#730;= 75&#730;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a kite ABCD, longer diagonal BD is drawn. If &#8736;ABD = 54&deg; and &#8736;ADB = 50&deg; &#8736;ABD = 54&deg;and &#8736;ADB=50&deg; , then what is the measure (in degrees) of the &#8736;DCB ?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2340;&#2306;&#2327; ABCD &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; BD &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;ABD = 54&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;ADB = 50&deg; &#8736;ABD = 54&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;ADB=50&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;DCB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; (&#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">108</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">108</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">76</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">76</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">54</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">54</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=174 height=193 id=\"Picture 27\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27168/image027.png\" ></p><p>In triangle ABD:</p><p>&#8736;ABD + &#8736;ADB + &#8736;BAD = 180&deg;</p><p>54&deg; + 50&deg; + &#8736;BAD = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BAD = 180&deg; - 54&deg; - 50&deg;</p><p>=&gt; 76&deg;</p><p>In kite ABCD, AB = AD and CB = CD (equal side pairs of a kite).</p><p>Therefore, &#8736;DCB = &#8736;BAD (because the diagonal BD bisects the kite symmetrically).</p><p>&#8736;DCB = 76&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>AB is parallel to DC in a trapezium ABCD. It is given that AB &gt; DC and the diagonals AC and BD intersect at O. If AO = 3x - 15, OB = x + 9, OC = x - 5 and OD = 5, and x has two values x<sub>1</sub> and x<sub>2</sub>, then the value of (x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; AB, DC &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; AB &gt; DC &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; AC &#2324;&#2352; BD, O &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AO = 3x - 15, OB = x + 9, OC = x - 5 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; OD = 5, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; x &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; x<sub>1</sub> &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; x<sub>2</sub> &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">45</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">61</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">61</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">73</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">73</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">56</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">56</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=357 height=200 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27705/image023.png\" ></p><p>In trapezium AB || DC, triangles AOB ~ COD: </p><p>AO/OC = BO/OD</p><p>(3x - 15) / (x - 5) = (x + 9) / 5 </p><p>(3x - 15) * 5 = (x + 9) * (x - 5) </p><p>15x - 75 = x<sup>2</sup> + 4x - 45 </p><p>x<sup>2</sup> - 11x + 30 = 0 </p><p>(x - 5)(x - 6) = 0 </p><p>x<sub>1</sub> = 5, x<sub>2</sub> = 6 </p><p>x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2 </sup>= 25 + 36 = 61</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a quadrilateral ABCD, the bisectors of &#8736;C and &#8736;D meet at point E. If &#8736;CED = 57&deg; and &#8736;A = 47&deg;, then the measure of &#8736;B is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;C &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;D &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; E &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;CED = 57&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;A = 47&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;B &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">47&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">47&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">67&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">67&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">77&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">77&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">57&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">57&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=278 height=158 id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21079/image041.png\"></p><p>In &#916;DEC:</p><p>&#8736;D/2 + &#8736;C/2 + &#8736;E = 180&deg; </p><p>&#8736;D + &#8736;C = 2 * (180&deg; - 57&deg;)</p><p>&#8736;D + &#8736;C = 246&deg; </p><p>Now, &#8736;A + &#8736;B + &#8736;C + &#8736;D = 360&deg; </p><p>47&deg; + &#8736;B + 246&deg; = 360&deg; </p><p>&#8736;B = 67&deg; </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The side MN of a parallelogram MNOP is produced to Q such that MN = N Q. PQ intersects ON at R. The point R divides ON in the ratio:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; MNOP &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; MN &#2325;&#2379; Q &#2340;&#2325; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; MN = N Q &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; PQ, ON &#2325;&#2379; R &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; R, ON &#2325;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3 : 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 : 1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2 : 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2 : 1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1 : 2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1 : 2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1 : 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1 : 1</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let M, N, O, P be the vertices of the parallelogram with MN and OP as opposite sides.</p><p><img width=263 height=90 id=\"Picture 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27162/image031.png\" ></p><p>Since MN = NQ, NQ is an extension of MN and thus MN = N Q.</p><p>Consider the triangle &#916;MNO and the line PQ intersecting ON at R, Since MN = NQ, triangle &#916;MNO and &#916;NQO are congruent by the Side-Side-Side (SSS) criterion.</p><p>Therefore, ON is bisected by R.</p><p>Hence, the point R divides ON in the ratio 1:1.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#916;XYZ and &#916;PQR are similar. XY : PQ = 6 : 1. Area of &#916;PQR is 6 cm<sup>2</sup>. What is the area of &#916;XYZ? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#916;XYZ &#2324;&#2352; &#916;PQR &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; XY : PQ = 6 : 1. &#916;PQR &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#916;XYZ &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">216 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">216 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">261 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">261 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>XY : PQ = 6 : 1</p><p>Area of &#916;PQR = 6 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Since, &#916;XYZ and &#916;PQR are similar =&gt;</p><p>Area(&#916;XYZ) / Area(&#916;PQR) = (XY/PQ)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of &#916;XYZ = (6/1)<sup>2</sup> * 6 = 216 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>PQ is parallel to SR in a trapezium PQRS. It is given that PQ &gt; SR and the diagonals PR and QS intersect at O. If PO = 3 x &#8722; 15, OQ = x + 9, OR = x &#8722; 5 and OS = 5 and x has two values x<sub>1</sub> and x<sub>2</sub>, then the value of (x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> - x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; PQRS &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; PQ, SR &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; PQ &gt; SR &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; PR &#2324;&#2352; QS, O &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PO = 3 x &#8722; 15, OQ = x + 9, OR = x &#8722; 5 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; OS = 5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; x &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; x<sub>1</sub> &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; x<sub>2</sub> &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> - x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">11</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=189 height=112 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27669/image029.png\" ></p><p>We know:-</p><p>In a trapezium with diagonals intersecting at O, the ratio of the segments of the diagonals is equal.</p><p>PO/OR=OQ/OS</p><p>Similar triangles: PO/OR = OQ/OS </p><p>(3x-15) / (x-5) = (x+9) / 5 </p><p>5(3x-15) = (x+9)(x-5) </p><p>15x - 75 = x&#178; + 4x - 45 </p><p>x&#178; - 11x + 30 = 0 </p><p>(x-5)(x-6) = 0 &rarr; x&#8321; = 6, x&#8322; = 5 </p><p>x&#8321;&#178; - x&#8322;&#178; = 36 - 25 = 11 </p><p>option (b) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a square ABCD, E is a point inside the square such that DDEC is an equilateral triangle. If E is joined to vertices A and B of the square, what is the degree measure of &#8736;AEB?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; ABCD &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; E &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; DDEC &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; E &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;AEB &#2325;&#2366; &#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">135&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">135&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">150&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">210&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">210&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">225&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">225&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=192 height=189 id=\"Picture 36\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24258/image036.png\" ></p><p>Since CDE is an equilateral triangle and ABCD is a square.</p><p>So, AB = BC = CD = AD = CE = DE</p><p>&#8736;CED = &#8736;CDE = &#8736;DCE = 60&deg;</p><p>&#8736;ADE = 90&deg; - &#8736;CDE = 90&deg; - 60&deg; = 30&deg;</p><p>In &#916;ADE: </p><p>&#8736;AED = &#8736;DAE = Let say x (AD = DE)</p><p>&#8736;AED + &#8736;DAE + &#8736;ADE = 180&deg;</p><p>x + x + 30&deg; = 180&deg;</p><p>x = 75&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AED = &#8736;BEC = x = 75&deg; [From the similarity]</p><p>&#8736;AED + &#8736;AEB + &#8736;BEC + &#8736;CED = 360&deg;</p><p>75&deg; + &#8736;AEB + 75&deg; + 60&deg; = 360&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AEB = 150&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the external angle of a regular polygon is 18&deg;, then the number of diagonals in this polygon is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 18&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">180</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">180</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">150</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">170</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">170</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">140</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">140</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Number of sides = 360&#730;/18&#730; = 20</p><p>Number of diagonals = 20*(20-3)/2 = 170</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>ABCD is a quadrilateral in which diagonal BD = 70 cm, AL &#8869; BD and CM &#8869; BD such that AL = 18 cm and CM = 20 cm. Find the area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the quadrilateral ABCD.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>ABCD &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; BD = 70 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, AL &#8869; BD &#2324;&#2352; CM &#8869; BD &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; AL = 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; CM = 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1310</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1310</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1300</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1300</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1330</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1330</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1320</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1320</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><b><img width=262 height=157 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27838/image004.png\"></b></p><p>Area of quadrilateral ABCD = Area of &#8736;ABD + area of &#8736;BCD</p><p>= &frac12; * 70 * 18 + &frac12; * 70 + 20</p><p>= 630 + 700</p><p>= 1330 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}